3079 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Throughout the term\054 you and your teammates will meet with local experts\054 take meaningful excursions\054 and engage regularly with local communities\056 It won\047t take long before you realize just how much your global experiences deepen your projects\047 meaning and amplify their impact\056\240\n\nFollowing the showcase\054 you\047ll meet one more time with the educators overseeing the project to reflect on your work\054 discuss what was learned and if expectations were met\054 and see how the skills you gained can be built upon in subsequent projects\056\n\nPersonal Projects\n\nPersonal Projects are the second type of PBL module at TGS\056 With the guidance of your academic mentor\054 you\047ll pursue projects that relate to personal interests\054 potential future paths\054 and service learning\056\n\nDuring these personal projects\054 you will formulate your own driving questions and select the learning targets you\047d like to focus on\056 It\047s an opportunity to pursue your passions or tackle a subject you\047d like to become more familiar with\056\n\nPersonal projects can take many forms\054 including exploring new technologies and how they could impact the world\054 crafting an original piece of art\054 working with a local organization to tackle a community need\054 or creating a paper or presentation to document your new understanding of an element of local culture or history\056\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n)
