  << /ActualText (Section 3\072 The Student Experience\n\nNow that you have an understanding of what project\055based learning is\054 we\047ll dive a bit deeper into the components of each\056 Every module\057project at TGS includes the following\072 a driving question\054 a process portfolio\054 learning targets\054 a project proposal\054 and the final product\056\240Here\047s a more detailed look at each\056\n\nThe Driving Question\n\nIn project\055based learning\054 a driving question is the central question of a module or personal project that guides students throughout the PBL process\056 It\047s a clear and engaging question that focuses a student\047s work toward solving a real\055world problem or answering a complex issue\056\240\n\nDriving questions are provocative\054 open\055ended\054 centered around a specific discipline\054 challenging\054 and aligned with curricular standards and frameworks\056 Most importantly\054 they help students stay on track by giving a clear purpose to the project\056\n\n\n)
