  << /ActualText (Learning Targets\n\nLearning targets are concrete goals\054 written in student\055friendly language\054 that succinctly describe what students will learn and be able to do by the end of a project\056 They are an essential component in planning and implementing modules or personal projects\056\n\nThere are ten different categories of learning targets at THINK Global School\054 each containing subcategories representing a diverse spectrum of learning objectives\056\n\nIn multidisciplinary environments like TGS\054 projects typically integrate learning targets from multiple categories\056 These targets provide focus\054 clarity\054 and serve as a basis for assessment\056 They also encourage student reflection\054 self\055assessment\054 and boost engagement by presenting clear and attainable goals\056\n\n\n)
